{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103693","id":2376316680,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6No7cI","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103693","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103693.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103693.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103693","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103693/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103693/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103693/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2b9d03e42fc4f09ebc33bc37c8b12aae699a4387","number":103693,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Optimize `Object::cast_to` for final classes by using `typeid` instead of `dynamic_cast`.","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`Object::cast_to` is used to check if an object is of a certain type. It uses RTTI (runtime type information) to do this (`dynamic_cast`). If the object type matches, it returns the pointer (reinterpreting the pointee), otherwise it returns a `nullptr`.\r\n\r\n### Explanation\r\n\r\nFor `final` classes, this operation is as easy as checking the type ID itself, because the type cannot be inherited from. The inheritance tree does not need to be checked, which is the slowest part of `dynamic_cast`.\r\nFor some reason, compilers (at least `clang`) are not optimizing this case. I'm not sure why. Either I'm missing something fundamental, or they just haven't managed to do it yet. In the future, this explicit check may become unnecessary.\r\n\r\n### Benchmarks\r\n\r\nI benchmarked a performance difference of at least `740x` (see misses; due to a call that prevents inlining the loop the hits are slower).\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Code</summary>\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nstruct Object {\r\n\tvirtual ~Object() = default;\r\n\tvirtual void a() {}\r\n};\r\n\r\nstruct B : public Object {\r\n\tvoid a() override {}\r\n};\r\n\r\nstruct C : public B {\r\n\tvoid a() override {}\r\n\t__attribute__ ((noinline)) void test() {}\r\n};\r\n\r\nstruct CF final : public B {\r\n\tvoid a() override {}\r\n\t__attribute__ ((noinline)) void test() {}\r\n};\r\n\r\ntemplate <typename T>\r\nstatic T *cast_to(Object *p_object) {\r\n\tif constexpr (std::is_final_v<T>) {\r\n\t\treturn (p_object && typeid(*p_object) == typeid(T)) ? static_cast<T *>(p_object) : nullptr;\r\n\t} else\r\n\t{\r\n\t\treturn dynamic_cast<T *>(p_object);\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n\r\ntemplate <typename T>\r\n__attribute__ ((noinline)) void test(Object *a) {\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 100000000; ++i) {\r\n\t\t__attribute__ ((noinline)) T *c = cast_to<T>(a);\r\n\t\tif (c) {\r\n\t\t\tc->test();\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n\r\ntemplate <typename T>\r\nstatic T *cast_to_old(Object *p_object) {\r\n\treturn dynamic_cast<T *>(p_object);\r\n}\r\n\r\ntemplate <typename T>\r\n__attribute__ ((noinline)) void test_old(Object *a) {\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 100000000; ++i) {\r\n\t\tT *c = cast_to_old<T>(a);\r\n\t\tif (c) {\r\n\t\t\tc->test();\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n\r\nint main()\r\n{\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\ttest<C>(new C());\r\n\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t}\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\ttest<C>(new B());\r\n\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t}\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\ttest<CF>(new CF());\r\n\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t}\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\ttest<CF>(new B());\r\n\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\ttest_old<C>(new C());\r\n\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t}\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\ttest_old<C>(new B());\r\n\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t}\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\ttest_old<CF>(new CF());\r\n\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t}\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\ttest_old<CF>(new B());\r\n\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nThis printed:\r\n```\r\n(new implementation)\r\n942ms (hit: cast C to C)\r\n754ms (miss: cast B to C)\r\n86ms (hit: cast C final to C final)\r\n0ms (miss: cast B to C final)\r\n\r\n(old implementation)\r\n917ms (hit: cast C to C)\r\n748ms (miss: cast B to C)\r\n910ms (hit: cast C final to C final)\r\n742ms (miss: cast B to C final)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Caveats\r\n\r\nIt's not clear whether we need this PR yet:\r\n\r\nCurrently, (almost?) no `Object` derived classes are even `final`.\r\nBut for a lot of existing `Object` classes, it doesn't make sense to derive from them. Some could probably be made `final` without much risk.\r\n\r\nAlso, it is unclear to me whether `dynamic_cast` is used in any performance critical functions. There _are_ around 2500 separate calls, but one would hope none are in per-tick functions.\r\n\r\nStill, I wanted to open this PR, just to show that this optimization is possible.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240